tor xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133298368,imgsize-30348.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[18-year-old Texas student builds ant-based digester, prototype is 83% efficient]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133298125.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A student developed an ant-based digester to process food waste efficiently.  This innovative system uses ants to break down organic materials, reducing landfill methane.  Experiments showed Camponotus castaneus ants consumed the most waste, proving effective.  Her prototype achieved an impressive eighty-three percent efficiency in initial tests.  This research offers a novel biological approach to managing discarded food materials.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-ananya-nagendra-the-18-year-old-texas-student-who-built-an-ant-based-digester-for-landfill-food-waste-tests-found-her-prototype-was-about-83-efficient/articleshow/133298125.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-ananya-nagendra-the-18-year-old-texas-student-who-built-an-ant-based-digester-for-landfill-food-waste-tests-found-her-prototype-was-about-83-efficient/articleshow/133298125.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T18:43:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133298195,imgsize-1438492.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kay Cottee sailed solo around the world in 189 days, making history]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133297589.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-1987-australian-sailor-kay-cottee-left-sydney-alone-in-a-37-foot-yacht-after-building-a-boat-charter-business-to-fund-her-dream-189-days-later-she-became-the-first-woman-to-sail-solo-nonstop-and-unassisted-around-the-world/articleshow/133297589.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-1987-australian-sailor-kay-cottee-left-sydney-alone-in-a-37-foot-yacht-after-building-a-boat-charter-business-to-fund-her-dream-189-days-later-she-became-the-first-woman-to-sail-solo-nonstop-and-unassisted-around-the-world/articleshow/133297589.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T18:31:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133297952,imgsize-66874.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[14-year-old becomes world Scrabble champion after moving to Australia]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133297284.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/14-year-old-dineth-fernando-moved-to-australia-seven-months-ago-and-studied-200-scrabble-words-a-day-recently-he-became-world-youth-scrabble-champion/articleshow/133297284.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/14-year-old-dineth-fernando-moved-to-australia-seven-months-ago-and-studied-200-scrabble-words-a-day-recently-he-became-world-youth-scrabble-champion/articleshow/133297284.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T18:11:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133297400,imgsize-840669.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Smithsonian uses X-rays, cups and 216-yard threads to find turtle nests; 13 of 16 were raided]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133296763.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Smithsonian scientists are utilising cutting-edge methods to identify turtle nesting sites, revealing that numerous nests fall prey to predators shortly after egg deposition. This alarming finding signals a crucial risk to the Eastern box turtle population. By monitoring turtle movements and nesting patterns, the research seeks to illuminate survival rates, which is vital for effective conservation initiatives.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/smithsonian-researchers-used-x-rays-plastic-cups-and-216-yard-spools-of-thread-to-find-wild-turtle-nests-predators-raided-13-of-16/articleshow/133296763.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/smithsonian-researchers-used-x-rays-plastic-cups-and-216-yard-spools-of-thread-to-find-wild-turtle-nests-predators-raided-13-of-16/articleshow/133296763.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T17:53:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133296919,imgsize-2162308.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['I don't have courage to take another loan': Indian student in Canada says going back home seems easier, sets up fundraiser]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133296750.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/i-dont-have-courage-to-take-another-loan-indian-student-in-canada-says-going-back-home-seems-easier-sets-up-fundraiser/articleshow/133296750.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/i-dont-have-courage-to-take-another-loan-indian-student-in-canada-says-going-back-home-seems-easier-sets-up-fundraiser/articleshow/133296750.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T17:48:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133296890,imgsize-55252.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Usain Bolt: "I stopped worrying about the start. The end is…"]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133296524.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/quote-of-the-day-by-usain-bolt-i-stopped-worrying-about-the-start-the-end-is-a-lesson-on-letting-go-of-a-shaky-beginning-and-focusing-on-the-finish/articleshow/133296524.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/quote-of-the-day-by-usain-bolt-i-stopped-worrying-about-the-start-the-end-is-a-lesson-on-letting-go-of-a-shaky-beginning-and-focusing-on-the-finish/articleshow/133296524.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T17:45:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133296758,imgsize-90117.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Woman donates $1 million to the teachers]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133295133.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A generous donation of one million dollars was given to teachers in California. One hundred educators in the Ross Valley School District received substantial bonuses. This significant gift came from a local resident concerned about teacher compensation. The teachers expressed deep gratitude for this unexpected and life-changing financial support. The donor hopes her action will inspire others to support public education.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/people/100-teachers-walked-into-a-meeting-expecting-an-ordinary-day-they-walked-out-with-over-9000-each-as-a-california-woman-offers-life-changing-bonuses-to-educators-struggling-with-low-salaries/articleshow/133295133.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/people/100-teachers-walked-into-a-meeting-expecting-an-ordinary-day-they-walked-out-with-over-9000-each-as-a-california-woman-offers-life-changing-bonuses-to-educators-struggling-with-low-salaries/articleshow/133295133.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T17:10:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133295712,imgsize-210115.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How 14-year-old Miles Wu is using origami to design stronger shelters]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133295421.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a groundbreaking study, young scholar Miles Wu delves into the use of origami techniques for emergency shelters. He meticulously examined fifty-four variations of the Miura-ori pattern and discovered that some designs could withstand more than nine thousand times their own weight. This ancient art form uncovers new possibilities for portable disaster relief structures. Wu’s research underscores the importance of geometric principles in enhancing the efficiency of materials.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-miles-wu-the-14-year-old-new-york-student-using-origami-to-explore-stronger-foldable-emergency-shelters/articleshow/133295421.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-miles-wu-the-14-year-old-new-york-student-using-origami-to-explore-stronger-foldable-emergency-shelters/articleshow/133295421.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T18:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133295637,imgsize-1038504.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Doja Cat’s response to a Twitch viewer asking about streaming quotas goes viral]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133293757.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Doja Cat recently explained her Twitch streaming motivations to fans. She clarified that she streams purely for enjoyment and personal satisfaction. The singer highlighted her elaborate room decor and outfits as proof of this. She stated that if quotas were her goal, she would appear in simple sweatpants. This approach shows her relaxed attitude towards the platform.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/doja-cats-response-to-a-twitch-viewer-asking-about-streaming-quotas-goes-viral/articleshow/133293757.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/doja-cats-response-to-a-twitch-viewer-asking-about-streaming-quotas-goes-viral/articleshow/133293757.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T15:59:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133293846,imgsize-672987.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘No. 1 goal is Iran can’t have nukes’: Trump as US-Iran 60-day deal deadline expires]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133293994.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/no-1-goal-is-iran-cant-have-nukes-trump-as-us-iran-60-day-deal-deadline-expires/articleshow/133293994.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/no-1-goal-is-iran-cant-have-nukes-trump-as-us-iran-60-day-deal-deadline-expires/articleshow/133293994.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T16:18:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133294351,imgsize-85538.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Arizona man, 88, and dog rescued after overnight monsoon mud ordeal with SOS text]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133293585.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A harrowing night unfolded for an 88-year-old man and his canine companion in Yavapai County when their vehicle became immobilized in thick mud from recent monsoon storms. An emergency SOS text sent out in distress helped authorities track them down. Fortunately, rescue teams reached them safely early Friday, aptly emphasizing the value of emergency communication features during critical situations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/arizona-man-88-and-his-dog-got-stuck-overnight-in-monsoon-mud-with-no-cell-service-how-one-emergency-sos-text-helped-save-them/articleshow/133293585.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/arizona-man-88-and-his-dog-got-stuck-overnight-in-monsoon-mud-with-no-cell-service-how-one-emergency-sos-text-helped-save-them/articleshow/133293585.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T16:09:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133293875,imgsize-1845390.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US Navy destroyer spent four days without toilets, AC, galley after power failure in South 